/-!
# The completed affine crystalline site and its pro-objects

Work in an affine crystalline situation `(A, I, γ, C)`. The *completed* affine crystalline
category `Cris^∧(C/A)` has as objects the divided power thickenings `(B, J, δ)` of `C` over
`A` whose underlying ring `B` is complete for the `p`-adic topology, and as morphisms the
divided power maps over `A` compatible with the identifications `C ≅ B/J`. Dropping the
completeness requirement and asking instead that `p` be nilpotent in `B` recovers the little
crystalline category `Cris(C/A)`, which is therefore the full subcategory of `Cris^∧(C/A)` on
the `p`-nilpotent objects: a ring in which `p` is nilpotent is automatically complete for the
`p`-adic topology.

The two categories are related by passing to finite level. For a completed thickening `B`,
all sufficiently high powers `(p)^e` are contained in `J` and are stable under the divided
powers, so each quotient `B/(p)^e` is an object of `Cris(C/A)`; completeness of `B` says that
`B` is the inverse limit of these quotients. Reading that inverse limit as a formal one
realises `Cris^∧(C/A)` inside the category of *pro-objects* of `Cris(C/A)`, and the main
result of this file is that the resulting functor is fully faithful. Full faithfulness is the
content that makes the identification usable: a map of pro-objects is, level by level, a
morphism out of some deep enough quotient of the source, and the compatible system of these
morphisms assembles — by completeness of the target — into a single divided power map.

A pro-object is implemented as an ind-object of the opposite category, i.e. by the covariant
functor `T ↦ colim_i Hom(B_i, T)`, using Mathlib's `IsIndObject`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.CompletedCrystallineThickening` — an object of `Cris^∧(C/A)`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedCrystallineThickening.Hom` — a morphism of `Cris^∧(C/A)`.
* `Crystalline.IsNilpotentCompleted` — the `p`-nilpotence property on completed thickenings.
* `Crystalline.NilpotentCompleted` — the full subcategory it cuts out.
* `Crystalline.FiniteLevelSystem` — the system of sufficiently deep crystalline quotients of
  a completed thickening, with its projections and transition maps.
* `Crystalline.ProCrystallineThickening` — the pro-objects of `Cris(C/A)`.
* `Crystalline.FiniteLevelSystem.diagram` — the inverse system of finite-level quotients.
* `Crystalline.proObject`, `Crystalline.proMap` — the pro-object of a finite-level system and
  the map of pro-objects induced by a morphism of completed thickenings.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.isAdicComplete_span_singleton_of_isNilpotent` — a ring is complete for the
  adic topology of a nilpotent principal ideal.
* `Crystalline.crystallineEquivalenceNilpotentCompleted` — `Cris(C/A)` is the full
  subcategory of `Cris^∧(C/A)` on the `p`-nilpotent objects.
* `Crystalline.exists_finiteLevelSystem` — a completed thickening is the inverse limit of its
  finite-level crystalline quotients.
* `Crystalline.completedCrystallineToPro` — the functor to pro-objects, together with the
  identifications describing it on objects and morphisms.
* `Crystalline.completedCrystallineToPro_fullyFaithful` — that functor is fully faithful.

## Implementation notes

As for the affine crystalline category, a surjection `B → C` with kernel `J` is encoded by a
bijective structural map `C → B/J`; this makes compatibility of morphisms expressible without
choosing an inverse. The `p`-adic topology on `B` is the adic topology for the principal ideal
generated by the image of the prime `p`.

The equivalence with the nilpotent objects is stated as a bundled equivalence together with
the identifications showing it preserves the underlying divided power ring, its maps from `A`
and `C`, and the underlying divided power maps; so it is the stated inclusion rather than an
arbitrary abstract equivalence. Morphism preservation is compared through the underlying
divided power maps, since the two categories use different structures for their morphisms.

Both `exists_finiteLevelSystem` and `completedCrystallineToPro` are stated existentially,
bundling the data with the identifications it must satisfy; this pins the construction down
to the intended one instead of asserting the bare existence of some functor.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07KH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07KH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05PX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05PX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

universe u v w

namespace Crystalline

/-- An object of the completed affine crystalline category `Cris^∧(C/A)`: a divided
power thickening whose underlying ring is complete for the `p`-adic topology. -/
@[stacks 07KH "completed_affine_crystalline_site"] public structure CompletedCrystallineThickening
    (S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}) where
  /-- The divided power ring `(B, J, δ)`. -/
  ring : _root_.DividedPowerRing.{w}
  /-- The divided power morphism `(A, I, γ) → (B, J, δ)`. -/
  fromBase : DividedPowers.DPMorphism S.A.dividedPowers ring.dividedPowers
  /-- The underlying ring `B` is complete for its `p`-adic topology. -/
  isComplete : IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {(S.p : ring)}) ring
  /-- The structural map `C → B/J`. -/
  toQuotient : S.C →+* ring ⧸ ring.ideal
  /-- The structural maps from `A` to `B/J` agree. -/
  commutes : (Ideal.Quotient.mk ring.ideal).comp fromBase.toRingHom =
    toQuotient.comp (algebraMap S.A S.C)
  /-- The structural map identifies `C` with `B/J`, equivalently encoding a surjection
  `B → C` whose kernel is `J`. -/
  toQuotient_bijective : Function.Bijective toQuotient

namespace CompletedCrystallineThickening

variable {S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}}
variable {X Y Z : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S}

/-- A morphism in `Cris^∧(C/A)` is a divided power map over `A` whose induced quotient
map is compatible with the structural maps from `C`. -/
@[ext, stacks 07KH "completed_affine_crystalline_site"] public structure Hom
    (X Y : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S) where
  /-- The underlying divided power morphism. -/
  hom : X.ring ⟶ Y.ring
  /-- The underlying morphism is over the fixed divided power ring `A`. -/
  fromBase_comp : hom.comp X.fromBase = Y.fromBase
  /-- The induced map on quotients commutes with the structural maps from `C`. -/
  toQuotient_comp : (DividedPowerRing.quotientRingHom hom).comp X.toQuotient = Y.toQuotient

/-- The category structure on the completed affine crystalline category `Cris^∧(C/A)`. -/
@[stacks 07KH "completed_affine_crystalline_site"] public instance :
    Category (CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S) where
  Hom := Hom
  id X :=
    { hom := CategoryStruct.id X.ring
      fromBase_comp := by ext; rfl
      toQuotient_comp := by simp }
  comp f g :=
    { hom := f.hom ≫ g.hom
      fromBase_comp := by rw [← g.fromBase_comp, ← f.fromBase_comp]; ext; rfl
      toQuotient_comp := by
        rw [DividedPowerRing.quotientRingHom_comp, RingHom.comp_assoc, f.toQuotient_comp,
          g.toQuotient_comp] }
  id_comp f := by apply Hom.ext; simp
  comp_id f := by apply Hom.ext; simp
  assoc f g h := by apply Hom.ext; simp

end CompletedCrystallineThickening

/-- The property defining the nilpotent objects of the completed crystalline category. -/
public abbrev IsNilpotentCompleted
    (S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}) :
    ObjectProperty
      (CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S) :=
  fun X => IsNilpotent (S.p : X.ring)

/-- The full subcategory of the completed crystalline category on nilpotent objects. -/
public abbrev NilpotentCompleted
    (S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}) :=
  (IsNilpotentCompleted.{u, v, w} S :
    ObjectProperty (CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u,
      v, w} S)).FullSubcategory

/-- A ring is complete for the adic topology of any nilpotent principal ideal. -/
public theorem isAdicComplete_span_singleton_of_isNilpotent
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (x : R) (hx : IsNilpotent x) :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {x}) R := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hx
  have hPow : (Ideal.span {x}) ^ N = (⊥ : Ideal R) := by
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_pow, hN]
    simp
  have hEq : ∀ a b : R, a ≡ b [SMOD (Ideal.span {x}) ^ N • (⊤ : Submodule R R)] → a = b :=
    fun a b h => by
      rw [SModEq.sub_mem, smul_eq_mul, Ideal.mul_top, hPow] at h
      exact sub_eq_zero.mp (by simpa using h)
  exact
    { toIsHausdorff := ⟨fun y hy => hEq y 0 (hy N)⟩
      toIsPrecomplete := ⟨fun f hf => by
        refine ⟨f N, fun n => ?_⟩
        by_cases hn : n ≤ N
        · exact hf hn
        · simp [hEq _ _ (hf (Nat.le_of_not_ge hn))]⟩ }

/-- The inclusion of the little crystalline category into the nilpotent objects of the
completed crystalline category: a thickening in which `p` is nilpotent is complete for the
`p`-adic topology, and its structural maps are unchanged. -/
public noncomputable def ordinaryCrystallineToNilpotentCompleted
    (S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}) :
    CrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S ⥤
      NilpotentCompleted.{u, v, w} S where
  obj X :=
    ⟨{ ring := X.1.ring
       fromBase := X.1.fromBase
       isComplete := isAdicComplete_span_singleton_of_isNilpotent (S.p : X.1.ring)
         X.1.prime_nilpotent
       toQuotient := X.1.toQuotient
       commutes := X.1.commutes
       toQuotient_bijective := X.2 }, X.1.prime_nilpotent⟩
  map f := ObjectProperty.homMk
    { hom := f.hom.hom
      fromBase_comp := f.hom.fromBase_comp
      toQuotient_comp := by
        simpa [DividedPowerRing.quotientRingHom]
          using f.hom.toQuotient_comp }
  map_id X := by ext; rfl
  map_comp f g := by ext; rfl

/-- The inverse of the inclusion above: a `p`-nilpotent object of the completed crystalline
category, read as an object of the little crystalline category. -/
public noncomputable def nilpotentCompletedToOrdinaryCrystalline
    (S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}) :
    NilpotentCompleted.{u, v, w} S ⥤
      CrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S where
  obj X :=
    ⟨{ ring := X.1.ring
       fromBase := X.1.fromBase
       prime_nilpotent := X.2
       toQuotient := X.1.toQuotient
       commutes := X.1.commutes }, X.1.toQuotient_bijective⟩
  map f := ObjectProperty.homMk
    { hom := f.hom.hom
      fromBase_comp := f.hom.fromBase_comp
      toQuotient_comp := by
        simpa [DividedPowerRing.quotientRingHom]
          using f.hom.toQuotient_comp }
  map_id X := by ext; rfl
  map_comp f g := by ext; rfl

/-- The ordinary crystalline category is canonically the full subcategory of the
completed crystalline category consisting of the `p`-nilpotent objects. -/
@[stacks 07KH "nilpotent_objects"]
public noncomputable def crystallineEquivalenceNilpotentCompleted
    (S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}) :
    { E : CrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S ≌ NilpotentCompleted.{u, v, w} S //
      (∀ X, (E.functor.obj X).1.ring = X.1.ring) ∧
      (∀ X, HEq (E.functor.obj X).1.fromBase X.1.fromBase) ∧
      (∀ X, HEq (E.functor.obj X).1.toQuotient X.1.toQuotient) ∧
      (∀ X Y (f : X ⟶ Y), HEq (E.functor.map f).hom.hom f.hom.hom) } := by
  let e : CrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S ≌
      NilpotentCompleted.{u, v, w} S :=
    { functor := ordinaryCrystallineToNilpotentCompleted S
      inverse := nilpotentCompletedToOrdinaryCrystalline S
      unitIso := NatIso.ofComponents fun _ => Iso.refl _
      counitIso := NatIso.ofComponents fun _ => Iso.refl _ }
  exact ⟨e, fun _ => rfl, fun _ => HEq.rfl, fun _ => HEq.rfl, fun _ _ f => by cases f; rfl⟩

section FiniteLevel

variable {S : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}}

/-- The data produced by cutting a completed thickening at one level: the quotient
thickening, the witness that it is crystalline, and the projection with its kernel and
compatibilities. -/
private structure FiniteLevelData
    (X : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S)
    (k : ℕ) (hcontained : DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ k ≤ X.ring.ideal)
    (hstable : X.ring.dividedPowers.IsSubDPIdeal
      (DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ k)) where
  object : DividedPowerThickening.{u, v, w} S
  crystalline : Function.Bijective object.toQuotient
  projection : DividedPowers.DPMorphism X.ring.dividedPowers object.ring.dividedPowers
  projection_surjective : Function.Surjective projection.toRingHom
  projection_ker : RingHom.ker projection.toRingHom =
    DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ k
  projection_fromBase : projection.comp X.fromBase = object.fromBase
  projection_toQuotient :
    (Ideal.quotientMap object.ring.ideal projection.toRingHom
      (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp projection.ideal_comp)).comp X.toQuotient = object.toQuotient

/-- The quotient of a completed thickening by `(p)^k`, as an object of the little
crystalline category together with the projection from the completed thickening. -/
private noncomputable def finiteLevelData
    (X : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S)
    (k : ℕ) (hcontained : DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ k ≤ X.ring.ideal)
    (hstable : X.ring.dividedPowers.IsSubDPIdeal
      (DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ k)) :
    FiniteLevelData X k hcontained hstable := by
  classical
  let J : Ideal X.ring := DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ k
  let qdp : DividedPowers (X.ring.ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)) :=
    DividedPowers.quotientDividedPowers X.ring.ideal X.ring.dividedPowers S.p k hcontained hstable
  let R : _root_.DividedPowerRing :=
    ⟨X.ring ⧸ J, X.ring.ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J), qdp⟩
  have hstable' : X.ring.dividedPowers.IsSubDPIdeal (J ⊓ X.ring.ideal) := by
    rwa [inf_eq_left.mpr hcontained]
  have hproj : X.ring.dividedPowers.IsDPMorphism R.dividedPowers (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) := by
    simpa [R, qdp, DividedPowers.quotientDividedPowers, J] using
      (DividedPowers.Quotient.isDPMorphism X.ring.dividedPowers hstable')
  let proj : DividedPowers.DPMorphism X.ring.dividedPowers R.dividedPowers :=
    DividedPowers.DPMorphism.mk' hproj
  let qmap : (X.ring ⧸ X.ring.ideal) →+* (R ⧸ R.ideal) :=
    Ideal.quotientMap R.ideal (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)
      (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp hproj.ideal_comp)
  have hcomap : (X.ring.ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)).comap
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) ≤ X.ring.ideal := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective (f := Ideal.Quotient.mk J)
      Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective X.ring.ideal, ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, Ideal.mk_ker]
    simp [J, sup_eq_left.mpr hcontained]
  have hqmap_inj : Function.Injective qmap := Ideal.quotientMap_injective' hcomap
  have hqmap_surj : Function.Surjective qmap :=
    Ideal.quotientMap_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  let f : S.C →+* R ⧸ R.ideal := qmap.comp X.toQuotient
  have hf : Function.Bijective f := by
    refine ⟨fun a b hab => X.toQuotient_bijective.injective (hqmap_inj hab), fun y => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hqmap_surj y
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := X.toQuotient_bijective.surjective z
    exact ⟨c, by simp [f, hc]⟩
  have hp : IsNilpotent (S.p : R) := by
    refine ⟨k, ?_⟩
    change (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (S.p : X.ring)) ^ k = 0
    rw [← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact Ideal.pow_mem_pow (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_singleton _)) _
  let T : DividedPowerThickening S :=
    { ring := R
      fromBase := proj.comp X.fromBase
      prime_nilpotent := hp
      toQuotient := f
      commutes := by
        change (Ideal.Quotient.mk R.ideal).comp
            ((Ideal.Quotient.mk J).comp X.fromBase.toRingHom) =
          qmap.comp (X.toQuotient.comp (algebraMap S.A S.C))
        rw [← RingHom.comp_assoc, ← Ideal.quotientMap_comp_mk
          (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp hproj.ideal_comp), RingHom.comp_assoc, X.commutes] }
  exact
    { object := T
      crystalline := hf
      projection := proj
      projection_surjective := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      projection_ker := by
        change RingHom.ker (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) = _
        rw [Ideal.mk_ker]
      projection_fromBase := rfl
      projection_toQuotient := rfl }

/-- The transition map between two quotients of `B` by powers of `(p)`. -/
private def finiteLevelMap
    (X : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S)
    (N e e' : ℕ) (h : e ≤ e') :
    (X.ring ⧸ DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ (N + e')) →+*
      (X.ring ⧸ DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ (N + e)) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.add_le_add_left h N))

/-- The transition maps between quotients by powers of `(p)` are compatible with the
quotient maps from `B`. -/
private theorem finiteLevelMap_mk
    (X : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S)
    (N e e' : ℕ) (h : e ≤ e') (x : X.ring) :
    finiteLevelMap X N e e' h
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ (N + e')) x) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ (N + e)) x :=
  rfl

/-- The system of sufficiently deep crystalline quotients of a completed thickening.
Every term is canonically the indicated quotient, and the transition maps commute
with the projections from the completed divided power ring. -/
public structure FiniteLevelSystem
    (X : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S)
    where
  cutoff : ℕ
  term : ℕ → CrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S
  projection (e : ℕ) : X.ring ⟶ (term e).1.ring
  projection_surjective (e : ℕ) : Function.Surjective (projection e)
  projection_ker (e : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (projection e).toRingHom =
      DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p ^ (cutoff + e)
  projection_fromBase (e : ℕ) :
    (projection e).comp X.fromBase = (term e).1.fromBase
  projection_toQuotient (e : ℕ) :
    (Ideal.quotientMap (term e).1.ring.ideal (projection e).toRingHom
      (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp (projection e).ideal_comp)).comp X.toQuotient =
        (term e).1.toQuotient
  transition {e e' : ℕ} (h : e ≤ e') : term e' ⟶ term e
  transition_projection {e e' : ℕ} (h : e ≤ e') :
    (transition h).1.hom.comp (projection e') = projection e
  transition_id (e : ℕ) : transition (le_refl e) = 𝟙 (term e)
  transition_comp {e e' e'' : ℕ} (h : e ≤ e') (h' : e' ≤ e'') :
    transition h' ≫ transition h = transition (h.trans h')
  limit_bijective :
    Function.Bijective
      (AdicCompletion.of (DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := X.ring) S.p) X.ring)

/-- A completed crystalline thickening is the inverse limit of its finite-level
crystalline quotients by powers of `p`. -/
@[stacks 07KH "finite_level_approximation"]
public theorem exists_finiteLevelSystem
    (X : CompletedCrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S) :
    Nonempty (FiniteLevelSystem X) := by
  classical
  have hpq : IsNilpotent (Ideal.Quotient.mk X.ring.ideal (S.p : X.ring)) := by
    have hcomm : X.toQuotient (S.p : S.C) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk X.ring.ideal (S.p : X.ring) := by
      simp
    rw [← hcomm]
    exact S.prime_nilpotent.map X.toQuotient
  let : Algebra (DividedPowers.IntegersAtPrime S.p) X.ring :=
    (X.fromBase.toRingHom.comp (algebraMap (DividedPowers.IntegersAtPrime S.p) S.A)).toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨N, hlevel, _hlimit⟩ :=
    DividedPowers.eventually_isDividedPowerCompletionLimit.{w, w}
      X.ring.ideal X.ring.dividedPowers S.p hpq
  let D (e : ℕ) := finiteLevelData X (N + e)
    (hlevel (N + e) (by omega)).1 (hlevel (N + e) (by omega)).2
  let term (e : ℕ) : CrystallineThickening.{u, v, w} S :=
    ⟨(D e).object, (D e).crystalline⟩
  let trans : {e e' : ℕ} → (h : e ≤ e') → term e' ⟶ term e := by
    intro e e' h
    let de' := D e'
    let de := D e
    let f := finiteLevelMap X N e e' h
    have hcomp : f.comp de'.projection.toRingHom = de.projection.toRingHom :=
      RingHom.ext (finiteLevelMap_mk X N e e' h)
    have hcompdp : X.ring.dividedPowers.IsDPMorphism de.object.ring.dividedPowers
        (f.comp de'.projection.toRingHom) := by
      rw [hcomp]
      exact de.projection.isDPMorphism
    have hdp : de'.object.ring.dividedPowers.IsDPMorphism de.object.ring.dividedPowers f :=
      DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.of_comp X.ring.dividedPowers
        de'.object.ring.dividedPowers de.object.ring.dividedPowers
        de'.projection.toRingHom f rfl
        de'.projection.isDPMorphism hcompdp
    let m := DividedPowers.DPMorphism.mk' hdp
    exact ⟨{
      hom := m
      fromBase_comp := by
        ext x
        change f (de'.object.fromBase x) = de.object.fromBase x
        rw [← de'.projection_fromBase, ← de.projection_fromBase]
        exact RingHom.congr_fun hcomp (X.fromBase x)
      toQuotient_comp := by
        change (DividedPowerRing.quotientRingHom m).comp
            de'.object.toQuotient = de.object.toQuotient
        rw [← de'.projection_toQuotient, ← de.projection_toQuotient]
        apply RingHom.ext
        intro c
        simp only [RingHom.comp_apply]
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (X.toQuotient c)
        rw [← ha]
        change Ideal.Quotient.mk de.object.ring.ideal
          (f (de'.projection.toRingHom a)) =
            Ideal.Quotient.mk de.object.ring.ideal (de.projection.toRingHom a)
        exact congrArg (Ideal.Quotient.mk de.object.ring.ideal) (RingHom.congr_fun hcomp a)
    }⟩
  refine ⟨{
    cutoff := N
    term := term
    projection := fun e => (D e).projection
    projection_surjective := fun e => (D e).projection_surjective
    projection_ker := fun e => by
      simpa [D, Nat.add_comm] using (D e).projection_ker
    projection_fromBase := fun e => (D e).projection_fromBase
    projection_toQuotient := fun e => (D e).projection_toQuotient
    transition := trans
    transition_projection := by
      intro e e' h
      ext x
      exact finiteLevelMap_mk X N e e' h x
    transition_id := by
      intro e
      apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
      apply DividedPowerThickening.Hom.ext
      ext x
      change finiteLevelMap X N e e (le_refl e) x = x
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
      exact finiteLevelMap_mk X N e e (le_refl e) a
    transition_comp := by
      intro e e' e'' h h'
      apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
      apply DividedPowerThickening.Hom.ext
      ext x
      change finiteLevelMap X N e e' h
          (finiteLevelMap X N e' e'' h' x) =
        finiteLevelMap X N e e'' (h.trans h') x
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
      simp only [finiteLevelMap_mk]
    limit_bijective := AdicCompletion.of_bijective_iff.mpr X.isComplete
  }⟩

end FiniteLevel

end Crystalline

